From 3888e0046427e76880e0cccce049a0369d8a4ba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David C. Manuelda" <StormByte@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 05:26:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] floor1: multiply negative post deviations instead of shifting

The floor post deviation mapping deliberately doubles a negative
deviation in its small-negative branch. A signed left shift is undefined
there. Use multiplication by two; floor quantization bounds keep the
result representable and the encoded mapping unchanged. Reproduced by
the existing Opus-to-Vorbis metadata test with UBSan.
---
 lib/floor1.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/floor1.c b/lib/floor1.c
index c4fe3ea..7cde16c 100644
--- a/lib/floor1.c
+++ b/lib/floor1.c
@@ -817,7 +817,7 @@ int floor1_encode(oggpack_buffer *opb,vorbis_block *vb,
           if(val<-headroom)
             val=headroom-val-1;
           else
-            val=-1-(val<<1);
+            val=-1-val*2;
         else
           if(val>=headroom)
             val= val+headroom;
